<title>NORWAY: DnB stock jump on Oslo Bourse.</title>
<headline>DnB stock jump on Oslo Bourse.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske Bank (DnB) was up 2.89 percent on the Oslo stock exchange in lively trade on Wednesday following the release of 1996 profits.</p>
<p>The share was was up 0.80 crownS att 28.50 crowns three hours into the session, at 1200 GMT. It was the third most traded share at about 34 million crowns.</p>
<p>DnB, Norway's biggest commercial bank, earlier on Wednesday announced that cost cuts and a healthy national economy helped lift 1996 net profits by 1.7 percent to 2.70 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
